Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attack
  In December 2025, a DDoS attack disrupted the national postal service of France and the postal service's bank. This resulted in the temporary shutdown of websites,
  and mobile apps. This slowed down parcel deliveries in the pre-Christmas rush.
Ransomware attack
  On the 15th of December 2025, a ransomware attack locked out the Venezuelan state oil company. This attack disrupted administrative systems, and halted oil deliveries.
  The company blamed the United States after one of its oil tankers was seized by the United States.
DDoS attack
  In November 2025, a Russian-aligned group performed a DDoS attack on Belgian telecom, health and defence websites. The attacks didn't cause any major or long lasting
  impacts, but it was part of a larger, politically motivated string of attacks on pro-Ukrainian members of the European Union.
Ransomware attack
  In October 2025, a ransomware group extracted 1.2 million patient records from SimonMed Imaging. The group demanded $1 million to delete the extracted data. 
Ransomware
  In September 2025, the Jaguar Land Rover IT network was infected with ransomware. This disrupted their manufacturing and retail operations. It is thought that this
  attack cost the company $1.9 billion, making it the most economically damaging cyber attack in the United Kingdom's history.

Source: https://www.csis.org/programs/strategic-technologies-program/significant-cyber-incidents
